- op: discuss  # 7107
  at: '2026-07-15T20:56:46Z'  # 7107
  by: agent  # 7107
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 7107
  clock: 3  # 7107
  nonce: '7107'  # 7107
  message: "DECISION 2026-07-15 (human-ratified, walked through step-by-step): KEEP shape_id, do NOT deprecate. Grounding in the ADRs+spec: spec §6 line 367 lists shape_id's Purpose as 'duplicate-code detection'; ADR-0035 §1 line 54 names shape_id + fingerprint 'the refactor-tracking instruments'; ADR-0014 defines it to detect structural changes (within-language). So shape_id is NOT a purposeless dead field — it is a populated (83%), fully-specified, spec-and-ADR-blessed field whose CONSUMER was never built. The honest fix for a write-only field with a documented, valuable purpose is to build the reader, not delete the field. Reframed from a deprecate-watch into this feature seed. Re-eval trigger flips to 'build-it-or-reconsider': revisit deprecation only if a future identity audit finds it still has no consumer AND the clone/refactoring-lead feature was affirmatively dropped from the roadmap. Prerequisite: WI-linon (Python shape_id collapses class/method/function + mis-hashes async def) must land first — a clone-detector on a buggy hash produces false clones. Parked feature sketch (not yet built): group nodes by (language, shape_id), surface the largest same-shape clusters as candidate copy-paste / extract-helper refactoring leads; within-language only per ADR-0014."  # 7107
