  nonce: 7bdf  # 7bdf
  message: "BUILT + CLOSED — PR c7826c11fc (merged to dev). Realized the human-ratified 'build the reader' disposition: new 'hypergumbo repeat-finder' read-view activates shape_id's one non-redundant capability over fingerprint (ADR-0035 §1, spec §367 duplicate-code detection). Groups symbols by (language, shape_id) — a cluster of >=2 is a structural-clone set (same skeleton, different names/literals), within-language per ADR-0014. Signal-dense defaults (owner-chosen): trivial clusters (shared cyclomatic complexity < --min-complexity, default 2) dropped; production clones (>=2 non-test members) are the headline, test-only clone clusters a labeled disclosure bucket (--include-tests); ranked by duplication burden (member count * representative LOC). text + json (view=repeat_finder envelope). Prereq WI-linon (kind-discriminated shape_id) landed first as required. BEHAVIORAL evidence (live self-corpus survey): 152 production clone clusters / 477 nodes, 0 kind-mixed (WI-linon holds), 1203 test-only clusters correctly bucketed away; top leads are GENUINE refactoring opportunities in hypergumbo itself (22 near-identical per-analyzer _get_identifier/_get_name/_extract_*_name functions; link_django/airflow dispatch pairs; CMake/Make analyzers). 24 unit tests, 100% coverage of new code; docs-prose gate + CLI flag matrix updated; CHANGELOG + spec §Commands documented. MVP scope: function/method/class clones, within-language; broader shape_id coverage tracked by the completeness siblings (WI-lutob/WI-luzut/WI-rokub/WI-sijug)."  # 7bdf
